       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 2,400 mg per dose four times daily is 9,600 mg/day. No indication supports that, and it would put the patient at serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and other toxicity. Each single dose is also three times the usual 800 mg maximum.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the usual outpatient maximum)\n\nIf there's a specific reason you need more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy. They can help with a multimodal regimen, for example scheduled acetaminophen or another agent alongside ibuprofen. If the \"2400 mg\" was meant as the daily total, tell me and I'll enter 600 mg four times daily."
      }
